{
  "run_id": "PMC12941970__broad__pcd_nocritic_PCD_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Polished CoCrFeMnNi has a native, unoptimized oxide layer.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::015::effect_of_control_functions_on_wear_rate"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled oxidation at 400–600 °C for a calibrated duration will form a nanocrystalline oxide film on CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC8448869::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxidation treatment will produce a chromium-enriched surface film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting oxide film will be continuous, uniformly distributed, and well adhered to the substrate.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::021::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting oxide film will be stable over the proposed service-temperature range.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide film will provide a lubricious, low-shear sliding interface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC11124323::web::021::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track",
        "PMC8448869::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide film will reduce direct metal-metal contact during sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::015::effect_of_control_functions_on_wear_rate"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing direct contact will limit adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::015::effect_of_control_functions_on_wear_rate"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide barrier will limit sliding-induced plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::015::effect_of_control_functions_on_wear_rate",
        "PMC8448869::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "An adhered oxide layer can lower friction by reducing interfacial shear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::021::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A protective oxidic surface layer can lower wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC11124323::web::021::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track",
        "PMC8448869::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treated CoCrFeMnNi alloy will have a coefficient of friction approximately 25–35% below that of the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treated CoCrFeMnNi alloy will have a significantly lower wear rate than the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC11124323::web::021::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track",
        "PMC8448869::web::017::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction and wear improvements will persist from room temperature to approximately 600 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermodynamic stability of the oxide film will be responsible for its broad-temperature effectiveness.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment's effectiveness depends on precise control of oxygen partial pressure, oxidation temperature, and duration.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An overly thick or unstable oxide film could undermine the tribological improvement.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::015::effect_of_control_functions_on_wear_rate"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The untreated alloy's uncontrolled native oxide results in higher friction and wear.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::015::effect_of_control_functions_on_wear_rate"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Processing parameters and test environments may change the magnitude of the improvement.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::015::effect_of_control_functions_on_wear_rate",
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Less than about 20% improvement in both friction coefficient and wear rate across the tested range is designated as a falsifying outcome.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
